Looking at this problem, I need to find all integers $n \ge 2$ such that $2013 \bmod n = n \bmod 3$.

**Key observation:** Since $n \bmod 3 \in \{0, 1, 2\}$, the remainder $2013 \bmod n$ must also be in $\{0, 1, 2\}$. This means $n$ divides $2013$, $2012$, or $2011$ (since $2013 \bmod n = r$ implies $n \mid (2013 - r)$).

